# Optional: enables real AI photo verification when scanning a clue location.
# Without this, photos are auto-accepted with a visible "AI verification disabled" notice.
# Get a key at https://console.groq.com/keys — this calls Groq's API directly from the
# browser, so the key ships in your client bundle. Fine for personal/local use, not for a
# publicly deployed multi-user app without a backend proxy.
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the vision model used for verification (defaults to qwen/qwen3.6-27b).
VITE_GROQ_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.6-27b

# Optional: switches the clue location picker (in Create Hunt) from the free Nominatim
# text search to Google Places Autocomplete + an interactive draggable-pin map. Without
# this, the free search is used and the app is fully usable either way.
# Get a key at https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis/credentials — enable
# "Maps JavaScript API" and "Places API" for it, then restrict the key under
# Application restrictions to your dev/prod domain(s). Requires a Google Cloud billing
# account (it includes a recurring monthly free credit, but calls beyond that are
# billed) — same client-side-key tradeoff as VITE_GROQ_API_KEY above.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Required: Base44 backend. Find your appId in the Base44 editor URL (the string
# between /apps/ and /editor/). Deliberately no API key here — do NOT add one.
# Base44's "api_key" header authenticates every request as the app owner (we verified
# this: it logs in as the owner account with zero password), so it must never ship in
# client-side code. Anonymous reads of public entities plus per-user login (email+password,
# with email OTP verification) is the safe pattern, and it's all this app uses.
VITE_BASE44_APP_ID=
